note """analysis check: NOT a diagnostic. `attempt` is READ by an earlier statement and WRITTEN by a later one. Flow-level vars carry Go's zero-value semantics, so reading before the first write is legal and the rule is ordering-free. This is the fixture an ordering check fires on."""
flow orders
import "github.com/acme/billing"
import "acme.dev/flows/audit"
var attempt int
source ingest Poll
transform charge billing.Charge from ingest
  reads attempt
transform backoff billing.Backoff from charge
  writes attempt
sink done audit.Store from backoff
